  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$  are\n\n$x\u2248$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\u2248$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{2}{3})=-0.729\\,727\u2026\u2248-0.7297\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-0.729\\,7$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.7297.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/92b256db68d09a07e5072d12cb18470e2c165b6f3c8aa29c6953d9aebb3b024e.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.7297 \\\\  & \u22483.8713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & =3.871\\,3-2\\pi \u2248-2.4119\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248-2.4,\\,x\u2248-0.7.\n$$",
